  -->position: another property used to move element within space
    ->absolute: if the element is assigned as "position absolute" it will be free and can be positined anywhere in the space.
    ->relative: it is made between parent and child element. it is assigned to parent element through which chils(being absolute) moves inside the parent element w.r.t. assigned dimensions.
    ->fixed: used to fix position of element if scroller is added or the website hi scrolled down

background--->
  it allow formatting the background of the element through several ways:
   ->image: added using url and set using three steps (syntax are given):
     -background: url()
     -background-size: cover/contain
     -background-position: right/left/center/bottom...
   ->color
   ->linear gradient
     syntax:
       background:linear gradient(specify_position, color1,color2)


flex: part of 'display' used to display diff child element in a line(side by side)
 --> adjusted using two axis:
     x-axis: main 
     y-axis:cross
     to adjust horizontally/in main axis use 'justify-content' 
     to adjust vertically/in cross axis use 'align-items'
  **flex is written in parent element. 
                 

pseudo elements: another great feature in css help in targeting particular things in an element.
 -it has five targetting properties:
  ::before         - helps in adding feature before any para/element
  ::after          - helps in adding properties after para/element
  ::first-line     - helps in targetting/formatting first line of para.
  ::first-letter   - helps in targetting/formatting first letter of para.
  ::selection      - helps in targetting/formatting selected text(by user) of para.
  
pseudo-classes: another feature of css helps in highlighting particular element select dynamically
 -it has four options:
  :hover          - used to format any element when cursor is moved to it
  :active         - used to highlight the element when it is clicked(mostly used in buttons element)
  :focus          - used to highlight element when working upon it(like in input elements)
  :nth-child(n)   -used to format 'n' line or elemnt in <p> tag.


Transform-origin: another great propertyof css helps in defining the rotating point of the div (default point is centre (50% 50%))